hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15446","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, Jamil narrated to me, and Mujahid informed us, from Nafi ibn Abd al-Harith, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Part of the happiness of a man is a righteous neighbor, and a comfortable mount, and a spacious dwelling."
"15447","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Habib, from Jamil, from Nafi ibn Abd al-Harith, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, and he mentioned the like of it."
"15448","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Abu Salamah, he said: Nafi ibn Abd al-Harith said: I went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until he entered a garden, so he said to me: Hold the gate for me. So he came until he sat upon the edge and let his feet down into the well. So the gate was knocked. I said: Who is this? He said: Abu Bakr. I said: O Messenger of Allah, this is Abu Bakr. He said: Admit him and give him glad tidings of Paradise. He said: So I admitted him and gave him glad tidings of Paradise. He said: So he entered and sat with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon the edge and let his feet down into the well. Then the gate was knocked, so I said: Who is this? So he said: Umar. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, this is Umar. He said: Admit him and give him glad tidings of Paradise. He said: So I admitted him and gave him glad tidings of Paradise. He said: So he entered and sat with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon the edge and let his feet down into the well. He said: Then the gate was knocked, so I said: Who is this? He said: Uthman. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, this is Uthman. He said: Admit him and give him glad tidings of Paradise, along with a trial. So I admitted him and gave him glad tidings of Paradise. So he sat with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon the edge and let his feet down into the well."
"15449","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Musa ibn Uqbah narrated to me, he said: I heard Abu Salamah narrating, and I know him only from Nafi ibn Abd al-Harith, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered a garden of the gardens of Madinah and sat upon the edge of the well. So Abu Bakr came seeking permission, so he said: Admit him and give him glad tidings of Paradise. Then Umar came seeking permission, so he said: Admit him and give him glad tidings of Paradise. Then Uthman came seeking permission, so he said: Admit him and give him glad tidings of Paradise, and he will meet a trial."
